Also ensure the code after we compute final score can be used.

Need to ensure we implement the overlay as part of render. Also maybe we need to adjust startLoop condition: currently they stop looping when phase == "gameover". In loop startLoop, after tick: they have if (phase !== "gameover") request next; else set loopId = null. This means after gameover, the loop stops and render will not be called again. In order to display the overlay, we could either still render the overlay before breaking out of the loop (so last frame draws overlay), then gameover stops further frames. That may be fine: on collision, checkCollisions sets phase = "gameover" and cancels the loop (with cancelAnimationFrame). That stops the loop by canceling the next tick. In startLoop tick, they call update/draw then schedule requestAnimationFrame if phase !== "gameover". However, they check after render: if (phase !== "gameover") request next; else loopId = null. So on gameover, loop will not request next frame, but we have already drawn overlay this tick if we include overlay. However, currently checkCollisions sets phase = "gameover" and also cancels the loop: inside checkCollisions they do:

phase = "gameover";
if (loopId !== null) cancelAnimationFrame(loopId);
loopId = null;

Thus at the moment collision is detected, loop is canceled mid-loop. However, this occurs inside update (when called before render). In tick, after update, they call render. After that they then schedule next tick based on phase. If phase == "gameover", they don't request next tick, but loopId already null.

